<item>
<title>Write-ahead logging</title>
<link>https://example.org/blog/series-wal/</link>
<pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
<guid>https://example.org/blog/series-wal/</guid>
<description>&lt;p&gt;The first part of the series carries the highest date, so a term page that&#xA;trusted Hugo&amp;rsquo;s default order would open the series here only by accident.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
<item>
<title>Multiversion concurrency control</title>
<link>https://example.org/blog/series-mvcc/</link>
<pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
<guid>https://example.org/blog/series-mvcc/</guid>
<description>&lt;p&gt;The second part is older than the first, which is the point: weight decides,&#xA;and the date only orders what carries no weight.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
<item>
<title>The buffer manager</title>
<link>https://example.org/blog/series-buffers/</link>
<pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
<guid>https://example.org/blog/series-buffers/</guid>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Last in reading order and second in alphabetical order: the fixture keeps path&#xA;order, date order, and weight order pulling in different directions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
<item>
<title>Vacuum and bloat</title>
<link>https://example.org/blog/series-vacuum/</link>
<pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
<guid>https://example.org/blog/series-vacuum/</guid>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Unweighted members follow every weighted one, in publication order &amp;ndash; oldest&#xA;first, which is the reverse of the order a term page hands them out.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
